  "claim_limit": "Only source-reported four condition-specific one-sample tests and ANCOVA slopes were re-extracted. Newly derived t/sqrt(df+1) is a within-study descriptive standardized departure, not a raw mean difference in OD600 or meta-analytic effect across independent studies. There are four experiment blocks and 12 replicates per specialist mixing ratio; the implied t-test n=74 or 72 is not the number of independent evolutionary origins. Missing original Dryad XLSX makes joint raw WT uncertainty, block-aware variance and effect size confidence intervals not identifiable here. Non-significant p=.073 is not equivalence. A fitted coexistence frequency is not a long-term evolutionary observation. No BITA startup cost K(u) or historical shared-to-split origin is measured."
